WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.229
Six neighbours give six tokens.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.463
Each holds eight numbers: its notepad.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.092
Layer norm reads a copy of the notepad.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.932
Subtract the mean, then divide by the spread.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:19.198
Attention is where tokens exchange information. Token j's weights produce an update.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.742
Write by adding: h prime equals h plus the update.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:29.838
Normalise again. The feed-forward network then handles each token alone, same weights.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.025
Its update is added too: h double prime.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.640
Two blocks give the input plus four updates.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.543
White outlines: the input, still inside.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.525
Now six blocks, with and without skips.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.904
Without skips, tokens collapse to one point. In the product, I is the skip.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.933
Each sublayer reads the stream, adds a correction, and passes it on.
